1
00:00:07,921 --> 00:00:13,206
The Life of Muhammadﷺ, The Madinan Period, Volume 1

2
00:00:13,386 --> 00:00:15,516
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:21,382 --> 00:00:24,000
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

4
00:00:24,068 --> 00:00:30,191
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْراَ

5
00:00:30,591 --> 00:00:32,680
In the beginning we say, Al-Hamdolillah(ألحمدلله),

6
00:00:33,073 --> 00:00:40,387
Who is allowing us to live these moments, with the best of His creation, Muhammadﷺ,

7
00:00:40,563 --> 00:00:46,550
it's such a great honor from Allahعَزّوجَلّ to allow us and give us that opportunity.

8
00:00:48,375 --> 00:00:51,124
We're carrying on with Ghazwat Badr(غزوة البدر).

9
00:00:52,023 --> 00:00:55,685
And we said that Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) was very alert,

10
00:00:56,473 --> 00:01:02,357
he, himself was scouting the area and he passed next to the wells of Badr(بدر).

11
00:01:03,037 --> 00:01:09,323
And he asked the people whom he saw there, who're drawing water from those wells.

12
00:01:10,236 --> 00:01:11,096
 He asked them,

13
00:01:11,449 --> 00:01:16,830
He said; Did you see anybody here, who's foreigner, whom you didn't distinguish.

14
00:01:17,553 --> 00:01:19,731
They said: We saw two men here.

15
00:01:20,136 --> 00:01:24,552
So, Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) went to the place, where their camels were.

16
00:01:25,193 --> 00:01:31,032
And he then held some of the camel manure in his hand, and he crushed it.

17
00:01:31,667 --> 00:01:38,096
And he said, these camels have been feeding crushed date seeds,

18
00:01:38,495 --> 00:01:41,227
and that is the animal feed of Madina.

19
00:01:41,849 --> 00:01:44,286
So he recognized that these two men came from Madina,

20
00:01:44,909 --> 00:01:47,013
and therefore he changed course.

21
00:01:48,388 --> 00:01:55,178
And he rushed towards the coast and was able to evade the Muslims.

22
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:59,922
And then he sends a letter back to Makkah,

23
00:02:01,407 --> 00:02:08,085
and he said: "You came out to do battle in order to protect your caravan, people and wealth,

24
00:02:08,426 --> 00:02:11,369
 Allah has now saved these, so go back."

25
00:02:12,166 --> 00:02:16,230
Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) said, there's no point now, in fighting, the caravan is safe.

26
00:02:17,348 --> 00:02:19,042
So, go back.!

27
00:02:19,987 --> 00:02:26,878
Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) said: "By Allah, we'll not turn around, until we reach Badr(بدر).

28
00:02:27,868 --> 00:02:32,184
And Badr(بدر) was a place, where the Arabs would hold the fair and a market each year,

29
00:02:32,256 --> 00:02:35,354
they would gather in that place and hold a fair.

30
00:02:35,778 --> 00:02:41,170
So, Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) went on, he said, we'll stay there three days slaughter some camels,

31
00:02:41,593 --> 00:02:46,645
eat well, drink wine, and the entertainers will play music for us.

32
00:02:47,298 --> 00:02:51,148
The Bedouin will get to hear of our journey and of our gathering there.

33
00:02:51,584 --> 00:02:53,236
And they will respect us for it.

34
00:02:53,490 --> 00:02:54,728
Let us proceed ahead.

35
00:02:55,748 --> 00:02:59,073
So, for Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل), it was a matter of flexing muscles.

36
00:02:59,404 --> 00:03:04,987
We'll go there, we'll celebrate, we'll drink wine, we'll have the slave girls, sing for us,

37
00:03:05,563 --> 00:03:12,188
and let all the Arabs come and see the strength of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and let them, fear us after that.

38
00:03:13,546 --> 00:03:15,083
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

39
00:03:15,261 --> 00:03:24,963
وَلَا تَكُونُوا كَالَّذِينَ خَرَجُوا مِنْ دِيَارِهِمْ بَطَرًا وَرِئَاءَ النَّاسِ

40
00:03:25,217 --> 00:03:36,019
وَرِئَاءَ النَّاسِ وَيَصُدُّونَ عَنْ سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ ۚ وَاللَّهُ بِمَا يَعْمَلُونَ مُحِيطٌ۝

41
00:03:36,743 --> 00:03:39,303
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

42
00:03:39,958 --> 00:03:45,830
And do not be like those, who came forth from their homes insolently,

43
00:03:46,323 --> 00:03:49,999
and to be seen by people and avert them from the way of Allah

44
00:03:50,229 --> 00:03:53,165
and Allah is encompassing of what they do.

45
00:03:53,612 --> 00:03:59,613
So, the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) came out with insolence and they came out to show off

46
00:04:00,145 --> 00:04:02,978
and to boast of their power and strength.

47
00:04:04,197 --> 00:04:11,775
Rasool Allah ﷺ, now realizing that the caravan is trying to get away,

48
00:04:12,139 --> 00:04:18,968
and that instead of facing a caravan guarded by 40 men, they might be facing an army of 1000 strong.

49
00:04:19,978 --> 00:04:22,036
Rasool Allah ﷺ held Shura(شورى)

50
00:04:22,504 --> 00:04:25,669
and he was asking the companions, What do you think?

51
00:04:26,721 --> 00:04:31,560
So, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) stood up and spoke, Umar Ibn Al-Khattabرضي الله عنه stood up and spoke.

52
00:04:32,056 --> 00:04:34,192
And then Al-Miqdaad(المقداد) stood up and spoke and

53
00:04:34,249 --> 00:04:36,853
Abdullah Bin Masoodرضي الله عنه said that,

54
00:04:37,008 --> 00:04:39,612
Al-Miqdaad(المقداد) stood up and spoke some words,

55
00:04:39,836 --> 00:04:45,034
I would sacrifice the world to be the one who spoke those words.

56
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:47,407
Al-Miqdaad(ألمقداد), he stood up and said;

57
00:04:47,518 --> 00:04:54,722
O Messenger of Allah, Go forth to what Allahعَزّوجَلّ has commanded you to do.

58
00:04:55,170 --> 00:05:02,288
And we are not going to tell you, like the children of Israel(اسرائيل) told Musaعليه السّلام;

59
00:05:02,737 --> 00:05:05,786
Go and fight with your Lord, we're going to stay here.

60
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:11,221
But we will fight in front of you and behind you and on your right and to your left,

61
00:05:12,047 --> 00:05:18,115
and we will say, Go forth and fight with Your Lord, we will fight with you.

62
00:05:19,166 --> 00:05:23,385
Rasool Allah ﷺ as it says in Al-Bukhari(اَلبُخَارِي), His face lit up,

63
00:05:24,483 --> 00:05:27,577
and it was shining, and he was happy, and he stood up.

64
00:05:29,562 --> 00:05:33,879
So, those words of Al-Miqdaadرضي الله عنه strengthen the Sahabah(صحابه).

65
00:05:34,119 --> 00:05:38,565
But that wasn't the case with all of them, not all of them had that idea on mind,

66
00:05:38,772 --> 00:05:42,911
see, because they didn't come out, prepared to fight a war.

67
00:05:43,442 --> 00:05:48,390
The reason why, they came out of Madina was to raid a caravan, so they were lightly armed.

68
00:05:48,650 --> 00:05:52,882
And mentally, they weren't prepared to face off an army.

69
00:05:53,128 --> 00:05:58,390
So, some of them were reluctant, and inside their hearts, many of them wanted to raid the caravan.

70
00:05:58,430 --> 00:06:00,940
They didn't really want to fight the army of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

71
00:06:01,081 --> 00:06:02,494
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

72
00:06:03,180 --> 00:06:06,773
By the way, how do we know what's in the hearts of people?

73
00:06:07,140 --> 00:06:11,254
See, that's the difference when we're dealing with history that is revealed in Qur'an,

74
00:06:11,358 --> 00:06:15,037
because Qur'an Allahعَزّوجَلّ knows what's in the hearts of people

75
00:06:15,505 --> 00:06:18,318
Unlike a historian writing a book about history,

76
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:20,405
he's going to go by what he sees,

77
00:06:20,445 --> 00:06:25,868
he doesn't really know what's in the insides of people in that particular era.

78
00:06:25,979 --> 00:06:27,306
 So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ tells us,

79
00:06:28,298 --> 00:06:34,306
it is just as when Your Lord brought you out of your home for the Battle of Badr(بدر) in truth.

80
00:06:34,704 --> 00:06:38,068
While indeed the party among the believers were unwilling,

81
00:06:38,703 --> 00:06:41,489
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is telling us and we wouldn't have known otherwise.

82
00:06:41,862 --> 00:06:43,269
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is telling us that

83
00:06:43,451 --> 00:06:44,420
some of the believers

84
00:06:44,460 --> 00:06:49,152
and by the way, here in the Battle of Badr(بدر), we're dealing with the cream of the crop, we're dealing with the best.

85
00:06:50,369 --> 00:06:52,531
Even though some of them were unwilling.

86
00:06:53,243 --> 00:06:57,644
Why? Because fighting is something disliked and here we're dealing with the first time,

87
00:06:57,869 --> 00:07:02,154
and there's some of them who maybe never met an enemy before.

88
00:07:02,475 --> 00:07:05,834
And there's that fear that could occur in a person,

89
00:07:06,020 --> 00:07:08,397
 when you're going to fight for the first time.

90
00:07:08,728 --> 00:07:12,635
So Allahعَزّوجَلّ is saying, a party among the believers were unwilling,

91
00:07:12,777 --> 00:07:16,759
 plus, fighting to start with Qitaal(قتال) is something disliked;

92
00:07:17,535 --> 00:07:22,048
كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْقِتَالُ وَهُوَ كُرْهٌ لَكُمْ ۖ

93
00:07:22,383 --> 00:07:29,258
وَعَسَىٰ أَنْ تَكْرَهُوا شَيْئًا وَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ ۖ

94
00:07:29,510 --> 00:07:36,150
وَعَسَىٰ أَنْ تُحِبُّوا شَيْئًا وَهُوَ شَرٌّ لَكُمْ ۗ

95
00:07:36,254 --> 00:07:41,594
وَاللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ وَأَنْتُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُونَ۝

96
00:07:42,088 --> 00:07:43,204
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

97
00:07:43,442 --> 00:07:47,585
"Fighting was prescribed on you, and you dislike it.

98
00:07:48,076 --> 00:07:49,245
But then Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

99
00:07:49,305 --> 00:07:51,976
وَعَسَىٰ أَنْ تَكْرَهُوا شَيْئًا وَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ ۖ

100
00:07:52,342 --> 00:07:55,337
but you might dislike something when it's good for you.

101
00:07:56,202 --> 00:07:57,519
Allahعَزّوجَلّ then says;

102
00:07:57,693 --> 00:08:02,248
يُجَادِلُونَكَ فِي الْحَقِّ بَعْدَمَا تَبَيَّنَ

103
00:08:02,478 --> 00:08:09,427
كَأَنَّمَا يُسَاقُونَ إِلَى الْمَوْتِ وَهُمْ يَنْظُرُونَ۝

104
00:08:10,577 --> 00:08:12,948
And then Allahعَزّوجَلّ says, Remember, O believers,

105
00:08:13,258 --> 00:08:17,727
when Allah promised you, one of the two groups that it would be yours,

106
00:08:17,973 --> 00:08:19,163
one of the two groups meaning,

107
00:08:19,330 --> 00:08:21,711
either the caravan, or to defeat the enemy,

108
00:08:22,037 --> 00:08:25,956
and you wish that the unarmed one would be yours,

109
00:08:26,027 --> 00:08:27,575
people wanted the caravan.

110
00:08:27,869 --> 00:08:30,360
And that caravan had the money of the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) in it,

111
00:08:30,544 --> 00:08:32,292
so they wanted it back.

112
00:08:32,577 --> 00:08:37,386
But Allah intended to establish the truth by His words

113
00:08:37,655 --> 00:08:39,718
and to eliminate the disbelievers,

114
00:08:40,213 --> 00:08:46,177
that He should establish the truth and abolish falsehood, even if the criminals disliked it.

115
00:08:46,638 --> 00:08:51,309
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ, had a plan, while the people had a plan,

116
00:08:51,890 --> 00:08:54,878
and the plan of Allahعَزّوجَلّ was greater than that of the people.

117
00:08:55,256 --> 00:09:01,225
The army of Rasool Allah ﷺ, some of them just wanted to raid that caravan and take over its wealth,

118
00:09:01,463 --> 00:09:07,282
 while Allahعَزّوجَلّ wanted this battle to be the first meeting between good and evil,

119
00:09:07,556 --> 00:09:12,522
and for it to be the day of Furqaan(فرقان), as we will see later on, it's the criterion.

120
00:09:14,212 --> 00:09:19,200
Rasool Allah ﷺ was gathering intelligence about the whereabouts of the army of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

121
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:24,640
and also the whereabouts of the caravan, if they would be able to lay their hands on it.

122
00:09:24,988 --> 00:09:28,900
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), they met with this old Bedouin,

123
00:09:28,940 --> 00:09:37,679
 this old man in the desert and Rasool Allah ﷺ asked him about the whereabouts of the army of Muhammadﷺ

124
00:09:37,719 --> 00:09:39,694
 and the whereabouts of the army of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

125
00:09:39,950 --> 00:09:42,484
So, the man said: "Who do you belong to?"

126
00:09:43,804 --> 00:09:46,433
I'm not going to tell you until you tell me who you are.?

127
00:09:47,007 --> 00:09:51,344
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him, if you tell us then we will tell you.

128
00:09:51,566 --> 00:09:55,282
The old man said: This for that, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes.

129
00:09:55,691 --> 00:09:56,973
So, the man said, fine.

130
00:09:58,156 --> 00:10:03,689
Muhammad(محمد) and his followers are at this place.

131
00:10:04,023 --> 00:10:07,731
And if the person who told me is telling me the truth.

132
00:10:08,096 --> 00:10:10,993
Now they would be in such and such place.

133
00:10:11,790 --> 00:10:16,605
And he gave the right place of Muhammadﷺ and his army.

134
00:10:16,984 --> 00:10:20,447
And then he said and the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were in such and such place.

135
00:10:20,864 --> 00:10:24,458
So, if the person who told me that is speaking the truth,

136
00:10:24,595 --> 00:10:27,228
now they would be in such and such place.

137
00:10:27,425 --> 00:10:30,889
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ here get some valuable information.

138
00:10:31,071 --> 00:10:38,397
And he can trust it because the man gave the right location of the army of Muhammadﷺ,

139
00:10:38,642 --> 00:10:42,564
even though he didn't know that he was speaking to Muhammad(صلواة الله وسلام عليه).

140
00:10:42,791 --> 00:10:44,795
So, that could be an indication that

141
00:10:44,875 --> 00:10:49,819
also the location that he's giving about the army of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) would be correct.

142
00:10:50,113 --> 00:10:54,389
So, now the Bedouins turn to ask Muhammadﷺ, Who are you?

143
00:10:54,596 --> 00:10:55,748
So, he says; Who are you?

144
00:10:55,874 --> 00:10:59,522
Muhammadﷺ says; We are from water and then he walks away.

145
00:11:00,264 --> 00:11:02,071
So, the old man is left to ask himself,

146
00:11:02,158 --> 00:11:05,016
What do you mean by water? Do you mean the water of Iraq?

147
00:11:05,629 --> 00:11:12,221
Because the Arabs would name some people according to the name of their wells, or their water source.

148
00:11:12,523 --> 00:11:15,210
 So since, in Iraq you have rivers,

149
00:11:15,577 --> 00:11:19,093
Rasool Allah ﷺ when he said that we are from Ma'a(ماء) we are from water.

150
00:11:19,165 --> 00:11:22,603
The man said: What do you mean by water? Do you mean the water of Iraq.?

151
00:11:22,973 --> 00:11:28,997
And Rasool Allah ﷺ just walked away, so that the man weren't ask him, some more investigative questions.

152
00:11:30,439 --> 00:11:33,958
What Rasool Allah ﷺ meant by that, was.?

153
00:11:34,152 --> 00:11:37,604
We're from water.! That's what we're created from,

154
00:11:38,164 --> 00:11:41,370
and Allahعَزّوجَلّ says in Qur'an that man is created from water.

155
00:11:44,666 --> 00:11:48,245
Rasool Allah ﷺ sends out Az-Zubair(أزبير) and Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب)

156
00:11:48,309 --> 00:11:53,007
and some other Sahabah(صحابه) scouting, the area, trying to gather information.

157
00:11:53,333 --> 00:11:58,748
So, they found a servant belonging to the army of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

158
00:11:59,018 --> 00:12:01,724
They arrest him and take him back.

159
00:12:02,422 --> 00:12:05,420
So, they brought him back while Rasool Allah ﷺ was praying.

160
00:12:06,620 --> 00:12:09,210
And then they would ask him, Who do you belong to?

161
00:12:09,551 --> 00:12:12,627
He would say, I belong to the army of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

162
00:12:12,809 --> 00:12:14,857
so they would beat him up badly,

163
00:12:15,892 --> 00:12:18,777
and they would ask him about the location of Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان)

164
00:12:18,817 --> 00:12:21,996
and this man doesn't know, he said I have no idea where Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) is.?

165
00:12:22,462 --> 00:12:24,822
So, they would tell him, Well, who do you know about.?

166
00:12:24,868 --> 00:12:29,309
 He said, I know the whereabouts of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل), Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(امية بن خلف) of Ut'ba Bin Rabiyah(عتبة بن ربيعة),

167
00:12:29,376 --> 00:12:33,089
and he's naming some of the prominent members of the army of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

168
00:12:33,728 --> 00:12:36,015
And they would beat him up and tell him where is Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان),

169
00:12:36,055 --> 00:12:38,134
so he say, okay, okay, I'll tell you about Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان).

170
00:12:38,246 --> 00:12:41,259
So, they'll stop beating him and then they'll tell him where is Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان).?

171
00:12:41,304 --> 00:12:42,375
He would say, I don't know.

172
00:12:43,248 --> 00:12:48,188
Now, the reason, why they were beating him to give them the location of Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) is.?

173
00:12:48,228 --> 00:12:51,184
 It shows you that they still wanted to know where the caravan is.!

174
00:12:51,802 --> 00:12:55,354
And they weren't happy when he told them that I belong to the army of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

175
00:12:56,036 --> 00:13:01,072
Rasool Allah ﷺ finished his Salah(صلاة) and told them, when he speaks the truth, you beat him.

176
00:13:01,754 --> 00:13:03,650
And when he lies, you leave him alone.

177
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:05,774
So, when he would say yes, I know where Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) is.

178
00:13:05,854 --> 00:13:07,171
They would leave him alone.

179
00:13:07,765 --> 00:13:10,751
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ went to interrogate him, himself.

180
00:13:11,092 --> 00:13:16,783
Because Sahabah رضي الله عنهم weren't really getting right information from him.

181
00:13:16,862 --> 00:13:19,387
 So, now Rasool Allah ﷺ walks up to the man, without beating him.

182
00:13:19,471 --> 00:13:20,640
 He just asks him.

183
00:13:20,950 --> 00:13:22,489
Tell me about the numbers.

184
00:13:22,950 --> 00:13:24,942
What's the number of the army?

185
00:13:25,418 --> 00:13:26,616
How many are they?

186
00:13:27,144 --> 00:13:30,035
So, the young man says, I have no idea.

187
00:13:30,451 --> 00:13:32,952
There are a lot, he'd say Katheer(كثير), they're a lot.

188
00:13:32,977 --> 00:13:36,372
Rasool Allah ﷺ wants to get some specific information.

189
00:13:36,538 --> 00:13:37,681
What does it mean a lot,

190
00:13:38,011 --> 00:13:39,118
Tell me how many they are?

191
00:13:39,166 --> 00:13:40,832
And this young man has no clue.

192
00:13:41,157 --> 00:13:43,856
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ asks him,

193
00:13:44,149 --> 00:13:46,669
How many camels do they slaughter every day?

194
00:13:47,438 --> 00:13:50,755
So, the man said, One day they would slaughter 10 camels

195
00:13:50,920 --> 00:13:52,845
the next day, they would slaughter nine.

196
00:13:53,041 --> 00:13:54,409
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

197
00:13:54,672 --> 00:13:56,939
اَلْقَوْمْ بَيْنَتْ ثَمِيْعَ وَالْاَلْفْ

198
00:13:57,395 --> 00:14:00,397
They are between 900 and 1000.

199
00:14:01,156 --> 00:14:07,979
Rasool Allah ﷺ asked him about how much meat they're consuming daily,

200
00:14:08,516 --> 00:14:14,375
And then, what from that he know, what the number of the army is.

201
00:14:14,696 --> 00:14:20,284
And he said they would be between Thousand and nine hundred and they were 950.

202
00:14:22,100 --> 00:14:24,434
The army was 950 strong.

203
00:14:25,185 --> 00:14:27,345
The cavalry was 200 strong.

204
00:14:27,504 --> 00:14:29,878
They had 600 coat Males.

205
00:14:30,306 --> 00:14:32,740
They had slave girls for entertainment,

206
00:14:33,232 --> 00:14:37,779
while the Muslim army was a little over 300.

207
00:14:38,122 --> 00:14:42,030
So, it's one third the number of the army of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

208
00:14:43,086 --> 00:14:51,677
Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) numbered 86, Al-Aos(ألأوس) were 61 and Al-Khazraj(ألخزرج) were 170.

209
00:14:52,135 --> 00:14:57,838
Now the reason, why the Aos(ألأوس) were fewer than Al-Khazraj(ألخزرج) Sixty one to 170.

210
00:14:58,107 --> 00:15:03,589
 Even though they are stronger and braver and as numerous as Al-Khazraj(ألخزرج) is

211
00:15:03,629 --> 00:15:09,259
because the dwellings of Al-Aos(ألأوس) were in the upper part of Madina

212
00:15:09,496 --> 00:15:15,737
and Rasool Allah ﷺ when he mobilized his army, he said, you only join us, if you have you ride ready.

213
00:15:15,946 --> 00:15:18,941
And because Al-Aos(ألأوس) were a bit far away.

214
00:15:19,069 --> 00:15:25,959
They weren't able to join in this army. So, that's why their number were fewer than Al-Khazraj(ألخزرج), in this battle.

215
00:15:26,907 --> 00:15:29,070
Al-Bara'a Bin Aazib رضي الله عنه, said;

216
00:15:29,506 --> 00:15:37,532
كُنَّا اَصْحَابَ مُحَمَّد نَتَحَدَّثُ اَنَّ عِدَّتَ اَصْحَابَ بَدْرٍ عَلَى عِدَّتِ اَصْحَا بِ طَالُوْطْ

217
00:15:37,889 --> 00:15:46,504
اَلَّذِيْنَ جَاوَزُوهُمْ مَعَه’ نَهَرْ وَلَمْ يُجَاوِزُمَعَه’ اِلَّا مُؤمِنْ بِضْعَتَ عَشَرْ وَثَلَا ث  مِيْعَةْ

218
00:15:46,737 --> 00:15:47,631
In Bukhari(البخاري).

219
00:15:47,964 --> 00:15:49,433
Al-Bara'a Bin Aazib(ألبرآء بن عازب) said;

220
00:15:49,644 --> 00:15:55,260
we the companions of Rasool Allah ﷺ when we'd talk about the Battle of Badr(بدر), we would say;

221
00:15:55,570 --> 00:15:59,868
 that the number of people who participated in the Battle of Badr(بدر)

222
00:16:00,153 --> 00:16:04,399
is equal to the number of people, who participated with Talut(طالوت),

223
00:16:04,987 --> 00:16:08,674
after they passed the test, after they passed the trial of the river,

224
00:16:08,880 --> 00:16:14,745
and the only ones who passed, were the believers, who were a little over 310.

225
00:16:16,114 --> 00:16:18,607
The fact that there is a correlation

226
00:16:19,060 --> 00:16:27,462
between the number of Muslims in the Battle of Badr(بدر) and the number of Bannu Israel(بنو إسرائيل) who participated with Talut(طالوت).

227
00:16:28,102 --> 00:16:33,547
And the fact that Al-Bara'a(ألبرآء) here mentions that these are the ones who passed the tests

228
00:16:33,674 --> 00:16:39,955
 and joined Talut(طالوت) tells you that the believers who are in the Battle of Badr(بدر) were also the best,

229
00:16:40,371 --> 00:16:45,761
these were the ones who passed the fittan(فتن), and the trials of this world.

230
00:16:46,571 --> 00:16:49,253
So, they are the best of the best.

231
00:16:50,373 --> 00:16:57,622
The exact numbers some give, the number is 317, Some give it as 319. It's close to this range.

232
00:16:58,257 --> 00:17:03,205
Rasool Allah ﷺ had banners, and that was his Sunnah(سنة) in every battle, flags

233
00:17:03,510 --> 00:17:05,018
the Muslims would have flags.

234
00:17:05,417 --> 00:17:13,939
They also had slogans that they would, or battle cries, and this is all to encourage the soldiers to fight.

235
00:17:14,390 --> 00:17:19,544
So, the banner was white, and it was given to Mus'ab Ibn Umair(مصعب إبن عمير).

236
00:17:19,953 --> 00:17:23,096
And then he also had two black flags.

237
00:17:23,390 --> 00:17:28,718
One of them was called Al-Uqaab(ألعقاب) and this was the standard that was carried by Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب).

238
00:17:28,914 --> 00:17:31,529
And the other one was given to one of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار),

239
00:17:31,767 --> 00:17:37,451
so Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) had a flag and Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار) had a flag and both of them were black.

240
00:17:37,825 --> 00:17:43,196
And then the army had a white flag and that was carried by  Mus'ab Ibn Umair(مصعب إبن عمير).

241
00:17:44,284 --> 00:17:46,983
The entire army had only two horses.

242
00:17:47,292 --> 00:17:51,896
One was for Az-Zubair(ألزبير) and the other one Al-Miqdaad Ibn Amr(ألمقداد إبن عمرو),

243
00:17:52,479 --> 00:17:54,582
and they had 70 camels.

244
00:17:55,267 --> 00:18:01,011
And we mentioned that every three would take turns on one camel.

245
00:18:02,519 --> 00:18:07,618
Rasool Allah ﷺ had Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) and Abu Lubabah(أبو لبابه) with him.

246
00:18:08,628 --> 00:18:15,435
And they offered to give up their turns for Rasool Allah ﷺ to ride and he said,

247
00:18:15,709 --> 00:18:20,734
You are no stronger than me, nor can I dispense with the reward more than you can.

248
00:18:21,312 --> 00:18:23,221
I need the Ajr(أجر) just like you do.

249
00:18:23,715 --> 00:18:25,676
And you're not stronger than me

250
00:18:26,049 --> 00:18:34,308
and Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) this was the leader of the Muslims and this was their teacher, Rasool Allah ﷺ.

251
00:18:34,729 --> 00:18:41,999
He wouldn't even allow his Sahabah to give up their returns for him.

252
00:18:43,130 --> 00:18:46,265
The Tawadh'ee(تواضع) the humbleness of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

253
00:18:47,556 --> 00:18:49,491
that's why they loved him so much.

254
00:18:49,825 --> 00:18:54,086
Like no followers loved any leader before.

255
00:18:54,659 --> 00:19:04,467
Never in the history of mankind, have we seen men who loved their leader as the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم love Muhammadﷺ.

256
00:19:06,159 --> 00:19:07,669
What about the choice of location?

257
00:19:07,765 --> 00:19:11,114
When Rasool Allah ﷺ chose the location of the army.

258
00:19:11,568 --> 00:19:15,618
Al-Habbab Ibn Munzir(ألحباب إبن اَلْمُنْذِر) one of Al-Ansaar رضي الله عنه,

259
00:19:16,309 --> 00:19:19,434
he went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said O, Messenger of Allah

260
00:19:19,981 --> 00:19:25,661
Is this the place about which Allah revealed to you,

261
00:19:26,173 --> 00:19:29,336
that we should not advance beyond nor stop before?

262
00:19:29,669 --> 00:19:32,526
Or is this a question of opinion, warfare and tactics?"

263
00:19:33,738 --> 00:19:36,076
And look at how he stated the question.

264
00:19:36,838 --> 00:19:37,573
He said;

265
00:19:37,692 --> 00:19:46,296
If this was a Wahii(وحي) from Allah, and we're not supposed to advance beyond or stay behind, then we're happy with it.

266
00:19:46,748 --> 00:19:50,638
But if it's a question of tactics, then I have something to say.

267
00:19:51,134 --> 00:19:52,780
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

268
00:19:53,058 --> 00:19:55,955
It's one of opinion warfare in tactics

269
00:19:56,602 --> 00:20:01,502
This is a choice based on my opinion of where we should be.

270
00:20:01,974 --> 00:20:05,610
Al-Mundhir(ألْمُنْذِرْ) said: well, O Messenger of Allah, this isn't the place to stop,

271
00:20:06,608 --> 00:20:12,516
We should go ahead till we get to the well nearest to their force, and stop there.

272
00:20:12,817 --> 00:20:18,792
We should then stop up, the wells behind it and build the cistern and fill it with water.

273
00:20:19,138 --> 00:20:22,371
Then we can fight them and have water to drink, while they have none.

274
00:20:23,028 --> 00:20:29,598
So, because you have these wells in Badr(بدر), We should take over all of the wells first and not allow them any access to them.

275
00:20:29,856 --> 00:20:31,686
So that, we'll be able to drink, while they won't.

276
00:20:31,749 --> 00:20:33,987
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: you have a good idea.

277
00:20:34,332 --> 00:20:39,442
And they advanced forward and had all of these wells behind them, behind their backs.

278
00:20:39,830 --> 00:20:44,196
And then they built a cistern, a pool filled it with water, so that they could drink from it.

279
00:20:45,298 --> 00:20:49,439
The night before the battle started Rasool Allah ﷺ saw a dream.

280
00:20:50,498 --> 00:20:57,471
And these are dreams that the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) see, which Allahعَزّوجَلّ strengthens them.

281
00:20:57,823 --> 00:21:03,314
Rasool Allah ﷺ saw the army of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) to be fewer than it really is.

282
00:21:04,488 --> 00:21:05,425
And why is that?

283
00:21:06,586 --> 00:21:11,249
Why would Allahعَزّوجَلّ make Muhammadﷺ see the army less than it really is?

284
00:21:11,407 --> 00:21:15,540
Isn't it better for him to see it, as it is?

285
00:21:15,866 --> 00:21:20,405
Well, Allahعَزّوجَلّ wants to strengthen the hearts of the believers.

286
00:21:20,603 --> 00:21:26,697
See, the army is three times the number of the Muslim army and that would weaken their morale.

287
00:21:26,768 --> 00:21:35,538
If the soldier is going to fight and he feels that he has no chance, he will be weak in the battlefield.

288
00:21:36,208 --> 00:21:39,431
So, they have to have hope that at least they have a chance to win.

289
00:21:40,108 --> 00:21:44,599
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ is showing the army of the enemy to be fewer than it really is.

290
00:21:45,359 --> 00:21:46,582
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

291
00:21:47,168 --> 00:21:52,118
إِذْ يُرِيكَهُمُ اللَّهُ فِي مَنَامِكَ قَلِيلًا ۖ

292
00:21:52,309 --> 00:21:56,333
وَلَوْ أَرَاكَهُمْ كَثِيرًا لَفَشِلْتُمْ

293
00:21:56,603 --> 00:22:03,515
لَفَشِلْتُمْ وَلَتَنَازَعْتُمْ فِي الْأَمْرِ وَلَٰكِنَّ اللَّهَ سَلَّمَ ۗ

294
00:22:03,814 --> 00:22:08,778
إِنَّهُ عَلِيمٌ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُورِ۝

295
00:22:08,990 --> 00:22:15,175
Remember O Muhammad(محمد), when Allah showed them to you, in your dream as few.

296
00:22:15,863 --> 00:22:18,522
And if he had shown them to you, as many,

297
00:22:18,971 --> 00:22:20,983
you believers would have lost courage,

298
00:22:21,312 --> 00:22:24,209
and would have disputed in the matter of whether to fight.

299
00:22:24,781 --> 00:22:29,738
But Allah saved you from that, indeed, He is knowing of that within the breasts

300
00:22:30,080 --> 00:22:34,760
So, this was to strengthen them and this happened the night before the battle

301
00:22:35,899 --> 00:22:42,364
The following day, in the morning, they had rain and this was not any season of rain.

302
00:22:43,515 --> 00:22:44,643
Ibn Is'haaq(ابن اسحاق) says;

303
00:22:44,738 --> 00:22:51,906
The valley was soft ground and the water from the sky dampen the earth for the Messenger of Allah and his force,

304
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:54,503
but did not impede their progress.

305
00:22:54,883 --> 00:22:59,852
But Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) had such rain fall upon them, that they could not move ahead.

306
00:23:00,891 --> 00:23:03,689
This is rain that showered on both,

307
00:23:04,061 --> 00:23:05,473
the Muslims and the non Muslims.

308
00:23:06,142 --> 00:23:10,931
But for the Muslims, it dampened the earth and it made it firm.

309
00:23:11,961 --> 00:23:16,935
While with the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), it became muddy and sticky and impeded their progress.

310
00:23:17,853 --> 00:23:21,615
So, the same rain had a different effect on both sides.

311
00:23:21,758 --> 00:23:23,867
It's a Mu'ajiza(معجزه) it's a miracle from Allahعَزّوجَلّ.
of them had wet dreams and they woke up in a state of impurity.

312
00:23:23,907 --> 00:23:28,248
Also some of the Muslims woke up in a state of impurity.

313
00:23:28,843 --> 00:23:33,894
Some of them had wet dreams and they woke up in  the state of impurity.

314
00:23:34,123 --> 00:23:38,612
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) Muslim doesn't really feel comfortable, when they're in the state of impurity,

315
00:23:38,652 --> 00:23:41,490
you know, you feel that you want to take a shower as soon as you can.

316
00:23:41,672 --> 00:23:47,950
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ despair them, that feeling of going into battle, while they feel that they are in the state of Najasa(نجاسه).

317
00:23:48,177 --> 00:23:51,672
Allahعَزّوجَلّ sends down this water to cleanse them.

318
00:23:52,301 --> 00:23:54,207
This is a spiritual cleansing for them,

319
00:23:54,405 --> 00:24:01,458
in addition to it, being water that would strengthen or make the earth firm, for them to march over.

320
00:24:02,236 --> 00:24:03,374
 Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

321
00:24:03,901 --> 00:24:10,697
إِذْ يُغَشِّيكُمُ النُّعَاسَ أَمَنَةً مِنْهُ وَيُنَزِّلُ عَلَيْكُمْ

322
00:24:11,086 --> 00:24:28,790
 وَيُنَزِّلُ عَلَيْكُمْ مِنَ السَّمَاءِ مَاءً لِيُطَهِّرَكُمْ بِهِ وَيُذْهِبَ عَنْكُمْ رِجْزَ الشَّيْطَانِ وَلِيَرْبِطَ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِكُمْ وَيُثَبِّتَ بِهِ الْأَقْدَامَ۝

323
00:24:29,001 --> 00:24:34,430
Remember when he overwhelmed with you, with drowsiness, giving security from Him

324
00:24:34,747 --> 00:24:39,871
 and sent down upon you, from the sky rain by which to purify you

325
00:24:40,101 --> 00:24:43,886
 and remove from you the evil suggestions of Satan,

326
00:24:44,215 --> 00:24:48,957
See because Shaytan(شيطان) was coming to them and giving them Waswash(وسوسه) you are impure.

327
00:24:49,410 --> 00:24:57,771
So Allahعَزّوجَلّ, removed that from them, and to make steadfast your hearts and plant firmly there by, your feet.

328
00:24:58,167 --> 00:25:01,524
So this rain had served all of those purposes.

329
00:25:03,295 --> 00:25:05,303
And also Allahعَزّوجَلّ says in the beginning of the Aayah(آية)

330
00:25:05,350 --> 00:25:09,224
إذْ يُغَشِّيكُمُ النُّعَاسَ أَمَنَةً مِنْهُ

331
00:25:09,458 --> 00:25:11,878
Remember when he overwhelmed you with drowsiness?

332
00:25:12,216 --> 00:25:18,283
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said; that night, the night right before the battle.

333
00:25:19,148 --> 00:25:20,454
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said;

334
00:25:20,751 --> 00:25:23,589
All of us were asleep, all of us fell asleep.

335
00:25:23,999 --> 00:25:26,978
And you know this is the night right before the battle.

336
00:25:27,391 --> 00:25:35,688
You would expect people to be anxious, worried, afraid, thinking a lot, they were asleep.

337
00:25:36,148 --> 00:25:41,632
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said; You could look at any one of us and we were all in deep sleep.

338
00:25:42,102 --> 00:25:45,356
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), that's why our scholars say that

339
00:25:45,893 --> 00:25:51,355
sleeping in battle or before battle is a sign of a Eeman(إيمان)

340
00:25:51,992 --> 00:25:56,640
and sleeping in Salah(صلاة) or during Salah(صلاة) is a sign of hypocrisy.

341
00:25:57,186 --> 00:26:03,743
The scholars would say that feeling drowsiness before battle or in battle is a sign of Eeman(إيمان)

342
00:26:03,974 --> 00:26:06,996
 because it shows the confidence of the heart,

343
00:26:07,461 --> 00:26:15,590
while feeling drowsiness or falling asleep in Salah(صلاة) is a sign of hypocrisy,

344
00:26:16,210 --> 00:26:18,409
As Allahعَزّوجَلّ says about the Munafiqeen(منافقين),

345
00:26:18,913 --> 00:26:22,552
when they go to pray, they go to pray in a state of laziness.

346
00:26:22,773 --> 00:26:25,280
كُسَالَىٰ يُرَاءُونَ النَّاسَ وَلَا يَذْكُرُونَ اللَّهَ إِلَّا قَلِيلً

347
00:26:25,325 --> 00:26:27,121
They don't mention the name of Allah frequently.

348
00:26:28,734 --> 00:26:30,897
So, the, Munafiqeen(منافقين) are just standing there in Salah(صلاة).

349
00:26:32,070 --> 00:26:35,356
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) says the only one who was awake, was Rasool Allah ﷺ,

350
00:26:35,396 --> 00:26:38,374
 Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) Rasool Ullah was standing and making Dua(دعا).

351
00:26:39,659 --> 00:26:44,342
And then Allahعَزّوجَلّ gives a description of the scene.

352
00:26:44,849 --> 00:26:54,742
إِذْ أَنْتُمْ بِالْعُدْوَةِ الدُّنْيَا وَهُمْ بِالْعُدْوَةِ الْقُصْوَىٰ وَالرَّكْبُ أَسْفَلَ مِنْكُمْ ۚ

353
00:26:55,036 --> 00:27:05,629
وَلَوْ تَوَاعَدْتُمْ لَاخْتَلَفْتُمْ فِي الْمِيعَادِ ۙ وَلَٰكِنْ لِيَقْضِيَ اللَّهُ أَمْرًا كَانَ مَفْعُولًا۝

354
00:27:05,816 --> 00:27:08,838
Remember when you were on the near side of the valley,

355
00:27:09,400 --> 00:27:15,134
and they were on the further side, and the caravan was lower in position, than you were.

356
00:27:16,191 --> 00:27:20,893
If you had made an appointment to meet, you would have missed the appointment.

