he said, well, they killed one of my sons and now they want me to ransom the other, let him stay with them.

547
00:41:00,407 --> 00:41:07,366
There was a member of one Arab tribe, who was a Muslim, who went to Makkah for Umrah(عمرة) or for pilgrimage.

548
00:41:08,057 --> 00:41:12,661
And you know, the people of Quraish(قريش) they would honor any pilgrim,

549
00:41:12,929 --> 00:41:19,354
they never violated any pilgrim, who would come to Makkah,

550
00:41:19,465 --> 00:41:23,687
they would respect them all, they would honor them, they would host them.

551
00:41:23,877 --> 00:41:28,330
 The honor of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) was based upon being generous to the pilgrims.

552
00:41:28,912 --> 00:41:33,456
So, here you have a Muslim going to Makkah, for Umrah(عمرة) or for Hajj(حَجْ),

553
00:41:33,990 --> 00:41:35,507
and he was taken as a prisoner.

554
00:41:35,793 --> 00:41:37,999
Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) took him as a prisoner.

555
00:41:38,325 --> 00:41:40,912
Now, Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ) says;

556
00:41:41,372 --> 00:41:45,788
Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) only ever treated well, those who came as pilgrims.

557
00:41:46,266 --> 00:41:48,945
This was the first time they would violate that law.

558
00:41:49,592 --> 00:41:51,995
Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) took him as a prisoner.

559
00:41:52,241 --> 00:41:56,241
So, then his family went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said; Our son is taken as a prisoner.

560
00:41:56,336 --> 00:42:00,055
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ ended up freeing the son of Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان),

561
00:42:00,336 --> 00:42:03,305
so that Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) would free this pilgrim.

562
00:42:03,910 --> 00:42:05,612
The reason why I'm bringing this up,

563
00:42:05,731 --> 00:42:10,334
is to show you that the kuffar(كفار) when they're dealing with the Muslims, they deal with a different standard.

564
00:42:10,716 --> 00:42:14,970
So, even though among the kuffar(كفار) you would have people who are anti war,

565
00:42:15,010 --> 00:42:19,248
 people who are peace activists, people who are moderate, people who are wise,

566
00:42:19,603 --> 00:42:24,113
people who represent voices of reason in times of war,

567
00:42:24,264 --> 00:42:29,679
but when it comes to Islam, things are different, because this is the truth.

568
00:42:29,719 --> 00:42:36,990
And Shaytan(شيطان) is working out there to convince his followers that they need to wipe out

569
00:42:37,600 --> 00:42:40,032
the followers of the religion of Allah from the face of the Earth.

570
00:42:40,561 --> 00:42:46,317
So, in the end, even though Ut'ba(عتبة) was one of their leaders, and he was trying to convince them to go back.

571
00:42:46,508 --> 00:42:50,762
And he stood up and spoke and told the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), some very convincing words.

572
00:42:50,952 --> 00:42:58,179
At the end of the day, it was Abu Jahal(ابوجهل), who carried the vote and the extremists won the election.

573
00:42:59,375 --> 00:43:04,043
Allahعَزّوجَلّ blessed the Muslims, as we said with sleeping the night before

574
00:43:04,068 --> 00:43:06,387
so they woke up active and ready to fight.

575
00:43:06,562 --> 00:43:08,768
The earth under them was firm.

576
00:43:09,402 --> 00:43:12,906
And He also blessed them with something else.

577
00:43:13,170 --> 00:43:19,238
Rasool Allah ﷺ saw the dream that the number of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) appears fewer than they really are.

578
00:43:19,564 --> 00:43:25,153
But when the Muslims actually saw the army of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), they also saw them less than they really were.

579
00:43:25,552 --> 00:43:26,949
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

580
00:43:27,484 --> 00:43:37,812
وَإِذْ يُرِيكُمُوهُمْ إِذِ الْتَقَيْتُمْ فِي أَعْيُنِكُمْ قَلِيلًا وَيُقَلِّلُكُمْ فِي أَعْيُنِهِمْ

581
00:43:38,042 --> 00:43:43,058
لِيَقْضِيَ اللَّهُ أَمْرًا كَانَ مَفْعُولًا ۗ

582
00:43:43,212 --> 00:43:48,458
وَإِلَى اللَّهِ تُرْجَعُ الْأُمُورُ۝

583
00:43:48,988 --> 00:43:52,031
And remember, when He showed them to you,

584
00:43:52,301 --> 00:43:58,359
when you met as few in your eyes, and He made you appear as few in their eyes,

585
00:43:58,623 --> 00:44:02,295
so that Allah might accomplish a matter already destined.

586
00:44:02,695 --> 00:44:05,418
And to Allah are all matters returned.

587
00:44:06,061 --> 00:44:13,242
So, we spoke about why Allah would make the enemy appear fewer in the eyes of the Muslims.

588
00:44:13,563 --> 00:44:19,615
But reverse also says that the Muslims appeared fewer in the eyes of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

589
00:44:19,686 --> 00:44:20,420
Why was that.?

590
00:44:21,569 --> 00:44:25,045
Allahعَزّوجَلّ gives us the explanation.

591
00:44:25,215 --> 00:44:27,298
لِيَقْضِيَ اللَّهُ أَمْرًا كَانَ مَفْعُولًا ۗ

592
00:44:27,739 --> 00:44:30,385
So, that Allah might accomplish a matter already destined.

593
00:44:30,690 --> 00:44:34,354
Allah wanted this war to happen, this battle to happen.

594
00:44:34,944 --> 00:44:43,067
So, when the enemies see the Muslims as fewer that would make them even more, eager to face the Muslims

595
00:44:43,162 --> 00:44:48,418
 because they would feel that they're so weak that they have a chance to wipe them out.

596
00:44:48,938 --> 00:44:52,111
But it also made them careless,

597
00:44:52,881 --> 00:44:59,775
because now they weren't preparing well or they were going into battle thinking that the Muslims were even less than 300.

598
00:45:00,743 --> 00:45:08,584
And when you feel that your opponent is weak, is too weak, then you go in with overconfidence.

599
00:45:09,468 --> 00:45:12,310
So, that was like a bait, to draw them in.

600
00:45:12,858 --> 00:45:17,839
But then as soon as they would face the Muslims and see that they have been deceived,

601
00:45:18,553 --> 00:45:20,641
 their morale will go down.

602
00:45:21,212 --> 00:45:28,302
Now with the Muslims, for them to see the enemy as fewer that will also give them confidence and strength to fight.

603
00:45:29,206 --> 00:45:32,492
So, What was the strategy of Rasool Allah ﷺ in fighting.?

604
00:45:32,944 --> 00:45:37,713
Rasool Allah ﷺ used the tactic that wasn't used by the Arabs before.

605
00:45:38,546 --> 00:45:42,174
It might have been used by other armies, in other nations

606
00:45:42,262 --> 00:45:45,674
 but it wasn't the method of fighting among the Arabs,

607
00:45:45,776 --> 00:45:48,980
the Arabs, their method of fighting was Al-Qarr, Wal-Farr(ألقر ولفر),

608
00:45:49,207 --> 00:45:54,935
Al-Qarr, Wal-Farr(ألقر ولفر)  is to raid or to attack and then withdraw

609
00:45:55,039 --> 00:45:57,722
to attack and withdraw to attack and withdraw.

610
00:45:58,079 --> 00:46:02,325
And it was pretty much disorganized attack.

611
00:46:03,532 --> 00:46:07,342
However, Rasool Allah ﷺ was employing the method of ranks,

612
00:46:07,774 --> 00:46:12,012
he would line up the army in two or three or more ranks,

613
00:46:12,226 --> 00:46:17,107
and then you would have the first rank are armed with lances.

614
00:46:18,076 --> 00:46:25,108
And you would have the ranks in the back armed with arrows or there would be the archers.

615
00:46:25,989 --> 00:46:28,354
So, the archers would fire from behind

616
00:46:28,718 --> 00:46:36,623
While the ranks in the front are fighting with their lances to prevent the advance of the attack of the cavalry.

617
00:46:37,198 --> 00:46:43,001
And as I said this was a new tactic employed by Rasool Allah ﷺ,

618
00:46:43,041 --> 00:46:45,015
it was new to the Arabs at least.

619
00:46:45,220 --> 00:46:49,667
And this is the way that Allah in Surat-Ul-Saff(سورة الصف), Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

620
00:46:49,897 --> 00:46:57,286
إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الَّذِينَ يُقَاتِلُونَ فِي سَبِيلِهِ صَفًّا

621
00:46:57,466 --> 00:47:03,648
صَفًّا كَأَنَّهُمْ بُنْيَانٌ مَرْصُوصٌ۝

622
00:47:04,025 --> 00:47:11,570
Indeed, Allah loves those who fight in His cause in a row as though they are a single structure, joined firmly.

623
00:47:12,207 --> 00:47:14,568
In this method, which is called in Arabic Zahaff(ضحف).

624
00:47:15,151 --> 00:47:21,230
This method of ranks which was the method probably employed by the Romans and the Persians.

625
00:47:21,667 --> 00:47:25,871
This method gives the leader greater control over the army

626
00:47:26,030 --> 00:47:30,244
rather than just attacking and withdrawing in a disorganized fashion.

627
00:47:30,668 --> 00:47:35,770
And that is how Rasool Allah ﷺ would fight in the majority of his battles.

628
00:47:37,201 --> 00:47:38,946
It's called As-Saff(ألصف).

629
00:47:40,030 --> 00:47:46,537
Rasool Allah ﷺ was also encouraging and inspiring the army.

630
00:47:47,428 --> 00:47:49,473
And that is an instruction from Allah,

631
00:47:49,513 --> 00:47:50,636
Allahعَزّوجَلّ told him;

632
00:47:51,286 --> 00:47:59,196
يَا أَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ حَرِّضِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ عَلَى الْقِتَالِ ۚ

633
00:47:59,498 --> 00:48:07,024
إِنْ يَكُنْ مِنْكُمْ عِشْرُونَ صَابِرُونَ يَغْلِبُوا مِائَتَيْنِ ۚ

634
00:48:07,333 --> 00:48:17,285
وَإِنْ يَكُنْ مِنْكُمْ مِائَةٌ يَغْلِبُوا أَلْفًا مِنَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا

635
00:48:17,753 --> 00:48:24,982
مِنَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا بِأَنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ لَا يَفْقَهُونَ۝

636
00:48:25,531 --> 00:48:29,910
O Prophet, urged the believers to battle, urge them, inspire them.

637
00:48:30,326 --> 00:48:35,227
If they are among you 20, who are steadfast, they will overcome 200.

638
00:48:35,616 --> 00:48:43,012
 And if they are among you 100, who are steadfast, they will overcome 1000 of those who have disbelieved

639
00:48:43,266 --> 00:48:45,850
 because they are a people who do not understand.

640
00:48:46,214 --> 00:48:52,319
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ stands up in front of the army and says; Every man who fights them bravely,

641
00:48:52,571 --> 00:48:57,774
and advances without retreating, will have Allah give him entry into paradise.

642
00:48:58,118 --> 00:49:02,467
And in Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم), Rasool Allah ﷺ stands up in front of the army and says,

643
00:49:02,617 --> 00:49:07,228
Go forth towards the garden the size of the heavens and earth combined.

644
00:49:07,360 --> 00:49:10,651
قُوْمُوْ اِلَى جَنَّتٍ اَرْضُهَا السَّمَوَاتِ وَالْاَرْضْ

645
00:49:11,710 --> 00:49:15,030
So, one of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, Umair Bin Hammam(عمير بن حمام) said;

646
00:49:15,094 --> 00:49:20,616
O Messenger of Allah, Could the garden really be the size of the heavens and the earth combined?

647
00:49:20,738 --> 00:49:22,164
Rasool Allah ﷺ said, yes.

648
00:49:22,394 --> 00:49:24,041
He said;Fine, fine,

649
00:49:24,100 --> 00:49:24,950
بخن بخن

650
00:49:25,409 --> 00:49:28,386
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said; What makes you say that, he said,

651
00:49:28,509 --> 00:49:32,914
O Messenger of Allah, it is only my hope of being one of its people.

652
00:49:33,065 --> 00:49:34,256
I want to be in Jannah(جنة).

653
00:49:34,472 --> 00:49:37,111
Rasool Allah ﷺ, said: You certainly will be.!

654
00:49:37,451 --> 00:49:40,444
So,  Umair Bin Hammam(عمير بن حمام) stands up, draws his sword.

655
00:49:40,788 --> 00:49:46,012
And then he has some dates, which she drew out of his pocket, and he started eating those dates.

656
00:49:46,084 --> 00:49:47,052
And then he said;

657
00:49:47,389 --> 00:49:51,310
If I live long enough to eat these dates, it would be a long life.

658
00:49:52,062 --> 00:49:54,952
He was so inspired by the words of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

659
00:49:55,112 --> 00:50:01,050
he was in such a hurry to die in the path of Allahعَزّوجَلّ, that he considered it, too long of a life,

660
00:50:01,334 --> 00:50:03,397
to even finish the dates in his hand

661
00:50:03,696 --> 00:50:06,127
and he rushed into the fray of battle.

662
00:50:06,471 --> 00:50:12,210
That is how inspired they were, based on the words of Mao'idha(مؤعظة), of reminder

663
00:50:12,392 --> 00:50:16,369
that they were hearing from Rasool Allah ﷺ.

664
00:50:18,305 --> 00:50:21,913
Rasool Allah ﷺ in the Battle Of Badr(بدر),

665
00:50:21,939 --> 00:50:26,193
 actually let me go carry on from some of the scenes that we're talking about.

666
00:50:26,328 --> 00:50:28,201
We'll mention the death of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل).

667
00:50:28,429 --> 00:50:31,219
Another important scene is what happened to Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(امية بن خلف).

668
00:50:32,072 --> 00:50:35,254
Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد ابن معاذ) said that I was friends with Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(امية بن خلف),

669
00:50:35,945 --> 00:50:41,246
and when he would visit Madina, he would stay with me and when I would visit Makkah, I would stay with him.

670
00:50:43,112 --> 00:50:48,243
So, Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد ابن معاذ) say that I visited Makkah and I stayed with Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(امية بن خلف),

671
00:50:48,307 --> 00:50:51,476
after Rasool Allah ﷺ has made Hijrah(هجرة) to Madina.

672
00:50:52,716 --> 00:51:00,437
So, I told him, I want you to find me a time, when it's not crowded,

673
00:51:00,982 --> 00:51:03,094
so that I can make Tawaf(طواف) around Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

674
00:51:04,643 --> 00:51:05,942
They went out to make Tawaf(طواف)

675
00:51:06,068 --> 00:51:08,736
and Abu Jahal(ابوجهل) sees Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد ابن معاذ).

676
00:51:09,237 --> 00:51:11,270
So, he asks Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(امية بن خلف), Who is this.?

677
00:51:11,310 --> 00:51:12,881
He said, this is Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد ابن معاذ),

678
00:51:13,366 --> 00:51:18,666
Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل), he said, I see that you are safe in Makkah.

679
00:51:19,469 --> 00:51:23,383
When you have given refuge to As-Subaa(ألصباء),

680
00:51:23,423 --> 00:51:26,661
this is a derogatory term that they would use against the Muslims.

681
00:51:27,062 --> 00:51:31,255
And you claim that you're going to support them and give them victory and protect them.

682
00:51:32,093 --> 00:51:37,379
If It wasn't that you are with Ummayyah(اُمَيَّه) with Abu Safwaan(ابوصفوان), I would have killed you.

683
00:51:37,976 --> 00:51:42,756
Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد ابن معاذ) responds back, his voice was loud.

684
00:51:42,827 --> 00:51:43,502
He said;

685
00:51:43,783 --> 00:51:47,861
If you do that, I'll do something that is worse for you.

686
00:51:47,981 --> 00:51:53,830
I will prevent your caravans from passing through Madina.

687
00:51:54,383 --> 00:51:57,306
So, Madina control the lifeline of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

688
00:51:57,891 --> 00:52:02,274
the route between Makkah and the Ash-Sham(ألشام).

689
00:52:02,938 --> 00:52:08,655
Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(اُمَيَّة بِنْ خَلَف) told Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعدابن معاذ), don't speak like that with Abul Hakam(أبو الحكم),

690
00:52:09,152 --> 00:52:11,221
because he's the chief of this valley.

691
00:52:11,949 --> 00:52:15,072
So, Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد ابن معاذ) said: Let's not talk about this no more.

692
00:52:15,600 --> 00:52:18,948
Plus, I've heard Rasool Allah ﷺ say that they're going to kill you.

693
00:52:19,645 --> 00:52:21,301
Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(اُمَيَّة بِنْ خَلَف) said; They're going to kill me?

694
00:52:21,341 --> 00:52:22,262
He said; Yes.

695
00:52:22,715 --> 00:52:26,943
Did he say if they're going to kill me in Makkah, or outside Makkah, Sa'ad(سعد) said; I don't know.

696
00:52:28,089 --> 00:52:31,207
Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(اُمَيَّة بِنْ خَلَف) went back to his home and he told his wife.

697
00:52:31,647 --> 00:52:34,425
Do you know what my friend from Madina told me.

698
00:52:34,630 --> 00:52:35,369
She said, what?

699
00:52:35,703 --> 00:52:39,405
He said, that Muhammad(محمد) promised his followers that he's gonna kill me.

700
00:52:40,415 --> 00:52:41,851
She said, Did he tell you where.?

701
00:52:41,891 --> 00:52:42,780
He said: No,

702
00:52:42,820 --> 00:52:45,407
I asked him whether it's in Makkah or outside Makkah.

703
00:52:45,700 --> 00:52:47,216
And he said he doesn't know.

704
00:52:47,526 --> 00:52:49,359
But I'm never going to leave Makkah then.

705
00:52:49,835 --> 00:52:53,573
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), they would accuse Rasool Allah ﷺ of being a liar,

706
00:52:53,612 --> 00:52:55,684
but then they would believe everything that he would say.

707
00:52:56,285 --> 00:53:01,274
So, it shows you that deep inside their hearts, they knew that he was Rasool Allah ﷺ,

708
00:53:02,405 --> 00:53:04,596
جَحَّدُوْ بِهَا وَسْتَيْقَنَتْهَا اَنْفُسُهُمْ

709
00:53:05,157 --> 00:53:11,123
They are rejecting the message, even though they believe that it is certainly true in their hearts.

710
00:53:12,017 --> 00:53:14,373
So, Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(اُميَّة بن خلف) says; I'm not going to leave Makkah.

711
00:53:15,325 --> 00:53:19,496
Now, when the call came to respond to the Battle of Badr(بدر).

712
00:53:19,936 --> 00:53:21,441
Ummayyah(اُمَيَّة) didn't want to leave.

713
00:53:22,526 --> 00:53:24,878
So, Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) brings him, a Mubkhara(مبخره),

714
00:53:24,918 --> 00:53:29,140
Mubkhara(مبخره) is this thing in which they burn inside it, the Ood(عود).

715
00:53:29,896 --> 00:53:33,504
So, he brought it to him and told them; Take it, because you're an old woman,

716
00:53:34,139 --> 00:53:36,282
so use this as old women do.

717
00:53:37,239 --> 00:53:42,163
Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) was insulting him and telling him that you're such a coward, you're going to stay behind with the women.

718
00:53:43,226 --> 00:53:45,104
Ummayyah(اُمَيَّة) was obviously insulted,

719
00:53:45,141 --> 00:53:51,068
and Abu Jahal(ابوجهل) kept on trying, until he was able to convince Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(اُميَّة بن خلف) to go out with them.

720
00:53:51,108 --> 00:53:53,626
Ummayyah(اُمَيَّة) went back home preparing to leave.

721
00:53:53,666 --> 00:53:58,920
His wife told him; Didn't you remember what your friend from Madina told you?

722
00:53:59,560 --> 00:54:00,798
He said; Yes, I do.

723
00:54:00,935 --> 00:54:04,046
But I'm just going to go, so far with them, then I'm going to come back.

724
00:54:04,371 --> 00:54:07,530
Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) said that whenever they would stop,

725
00:54:07,649 --> 00:54:10,865
he would make the intentions that the next stop would be, the last stop

726
00:54:11,270 --> 00:54:15,409
until he ended up entering the fray of the battle, himself.

727
00:54:16,490 --> 00:54:23,186
So, Ummayyah(اُمَيَّة) ended up being captured by Abdur-Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدألرحمن إبن عوف).

728
00:54:23,322 --> 00:54:24,062
How did it happen?

729
00:54:24,162 --> 00:54:26,488
Abdur-Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدألرحمن إبن عوف) is narrating the story himself.

730
00:54:26,937 --> 00:54:33,114
He said: I had a bunch of coat males with me, armor.

731
00:54:33,750 --> 00:54:39,528
And these are pretty expensive, and he has collected them one by one, as booty.

732
00:54:40,140 --> 00:54:45,318
And then Ummayyah(اُمَيَّة) sees him and says, O Abd Amr(عبدعمرو),

733
00:54:45,800 --> 00:54:47,703
Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) said:  I didn't respond.

734
00:54:48,155 --> 00:54:51,846
See! Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) and Ummayyah(اُمَيَّة) were friends in Makkah.

735
00:54:52,390 --> 00:54:54,723
And the name of Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) was Abd Amr(عبدعمرو),

736
00:54:55,490 --> 00:54:58,107
when he became Muslim, he changed his name to Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن).

737
00:54:58,960 --> 00:55:02,580
Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) said: when Ummayyah(اُمَيَّة) would call me, Abd Amr(عبدعمرو), I wouldn't respond.

738
00:55:03,311 --> 00:55:08,068
So, Ummayyah(اُمَيَّة) told him, when I call you Abd Amr(عبدعمرو) you refused to respond back.

739
00:55:08,571 --> 00:55:12,338
And I do not recognize, Ar-Rahman(ألرحمن), so I cannot call you Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن).

740
00:55:13,131 --> 00:55:17,000
So, how about you choose for yourself a name, just for me and you.

741
00:55:17,505 --> 00:55:20,394
So, Abdur-Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدألرحمن إبن عوف) said; Well you go ahead and choose the name.

742
00:55:20,572 --> 00:55:24,774
He said, I'll call you Abdul Illah(عبداله), the servant of God.

743
00:55:25,806 --> 00:55:26,788
So they agreed.

744
00:55:27,072 --> 00:55:30,691
So, whenever Ummayyah(اُمَيَّة) would meet Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن), he would say, Abdul Illah(عبداله),

745
00:55:31,515 --> 00:55:34,477
because the Mushriqeen(مشركين) of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) did not recognize, Ar-Rahman(ألرحمن).

746
00:55:35,205 --> 00:55:39,544
That's in one narration, in another narration it says that Abdur-Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدألرحمن إبن عوف) said that

747
00:55:39,860 --> 00:55:44,762
I had an agreement with Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(اُمَيَّة بِنْ خَلَف) that I will take care of his business interests

748
00:55:44,802 --> 00:55:45,882
 and this is in Bukhari(بخاريْ),

749
00:55:45,975 --> 00:55:48,306
I'll take care of his business interest in Madina,

750
00:55:48,524 --> 00:55:51,520
while he'll take care of my business interests in Makkah.

751
00:55:52,054 --> 00:55:56,058
Abdur-Rahman(عبدألرحمن إبن عوف) said: I didn't respond back to Ummayyah(اُمَيَّة),

752
00:55:56,098 --> 00:55:58,506
when he said Abd Amr(عبدعمرو) and then he said, Abdul Illah(عبداله),

753
00:55:58,546 --> 00:56:01,085
so I responded back to him, and he said,

754
00:56:01,707 --> 00:56:05,723
Do you want something better for you than those coat males that you're carrying?"

755
00:56:05,981 --> 00:56:07,328
Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) said: What is it?

756
00:56:07,588 --> 00:56:09,268
He said: Me and my son.

757
00:56:10,068 --> 00:56:11,996
Obviously, Ummayyah(اُمَيَّة) is rich,

758
00:56:12,405 --> 00:56:14,195
so his ransom will fetch a lot of money.

759
00:56:14,830 --> 00:56:16,298
Same with his son, Ali(علي).

760
00:56:16,933 --> 00:56:21,159
So Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) said: I threw the armor from my hand,

761
00:56:21,526 --> 00:56:25,312
and I held Ummayyah(اُمَيَّه), and his son Ali(علي), in both of my hands.

762
00:56:25,394 --> 00:56:27,839
So now, they are his prisoners of war.

763
00:56:28,316 --> 00:56:29,744
And he's the one who's holding them.

764
00:56:30,251 --> 00:56:33,057
Therefore, he is the one who will get the ransom

765
00:56:33,097 --> 00:56:39,208
since according to the tradition, if you are the one who capture somebody, you get the ransom for him.

766
00:56:39,800 --> 00:56:41,925
So, it was a better deal for Abdur-Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدألرحمن إبن عوف)

767
00:56:42,342 --> 00:56:45,857
However, someone spots Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(اُمَيَّة بِنْ خَلَف) and who was it?

768
00:56:46,642 --> 00:56:47,515
Bilal(بلال),

769
00:56:47,679 --> 00:56:51,504
Bilal Bin Rabah(بلال بن رباح), the former slave of Ummayyah(اُمَيَّة),

770
00:56:52,278 --> 00:56:54,540
the one, who was tortured by Ummayyah(اُمَيَّة),

771
00:56:55,820 --> 00:56:59,441
and the story of the torture of Bilal(بلال) is famous, you all know it.

772
00:57:00,457 --> 00:57:04,964
So Bilal Bin Rabah(بلال بن رباح), when he sees Abdur-Rahman Ibn Auf(ألرحمن إبن عوف), he said;

773
00:57:05,150 --> 00:57:06,643
اُمَيَّةْ رَاْسُ الْكُفْرْ

774
00:57:06,910 --> 00:57:10,602
Ummayyah(اُمَيَّة), the head of the disbelievers.

775
00:57:11,300 --> 00:57:12,214
Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) said;

776
00:57:12,238 --> 00:57:12,973
يَا بِلَالْ

777
00:57:13,143 --> 00:57:16,478
Hey, Bilal(بلال)! He is my prisoner.

778
00:57:17,288 --> 00:57:18,076
Bilal(بلال) says;

779
00:57:18,100 --> 00:57:19,508
لَا نَجَوْتُ اِنْ نَجَا

780
00:57:19,971 --> 00:57:21,956
I will not live, if he does.

781
00:57:22,432 --> 00:57:23,653
Abdur-Rahman Bin Auf(عبد ألرحمن إبن عوف) said;

782
00:57:23,694 --> 00:57:25,647
Listen Bilal(بلال), he is my prisoner.

783
00:57:26,021 --> 00:57:30,195
Bilal(بلال), when he realizes that Abdur-Rahman(عبدالرحمن) is not willing to give him up.

784
00:57:30,549 --> 00:57:32,950
Bilal(بلال) goes to some of the Ansaar(أنْصَار) and tells them

785
00:57:33,286 --> 00:57:36,944
that man is Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(اُمَيَّة بِنْ خَلَف), Ra'as-Ul-Kuffr(رأس الكفر)

786
00:57:37,544 --> 00:57:39,964
That man is Ummayyah(اُمَيَّة), the head of the disbelievers.

787
00:57:40,084 --> 00:57:41,974
 I'm not gonna live, if he does.

788
00:57:42,779 --> 00:57:46,918
Abdur-Rahman Bin Auf(عبد ألرحمن إبن عوف) said: "So they pounced on us, they attacked.

789
00:57:47,514 --> 00:57:53,254
Now he said they enclosed us and I felt that I wouldn't be able to defend them.

790
00:57:53,325 --> 00:57:59,342
So, what I did is I released Ali(علي), to get them busy with him.

791
00:57:59,699 --> 00:58:01,584
And then I told Ummayyah(اُمَيَّة) to run with me.

792
00:58:02,459 --> 00:58:06,295
So, they attacked Ali(علي) and they killed him, they cut them into pieces.

793
00:58:06,989 --> 00:58:10,346
And I was telling Ummayyah(اُمَيَّة) to run but he was a heavy man,

794
00:58:10,809 --> 00:58:12,602
so they ended up catching up with us.

795
00:58:12,793 --> 00:58:18,125
So, I told him to lay down, and then I jumped over him, to protect him with my own body.

796
00:58:18,589 --> 00:58:22,905
He said, so the swords of the Ansaar(أنْصَار) were digging deep under me

797
00:58:23,342 --> 00:58:24,347
tearing him apart.

798
00:58:24,664 --> 00:58:27,474
In fact, one of them even injured me in my foot.

799
00:58:27,746 --> 00:58:29,950
And the narrator of this Hadith(حديث) would say;

800
00:58:29,990 --> 00:58:34,996
Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) would show us the scar that was left, by the swords of the Sahabah.

801
00:58:35,530 --> 00:58:37,294
Abdur-Rahman Bin Auf(عبد ألرحمن إبن عوف) would then say,

802
00:58:37,520 --> 00:58:38,917
رحمه الله بلال

803
00:58:39,123 --> 00:58:44,654
may Allah Have mercy on Bilal(بلال), He made me lose my armor and lose my prisoners, I lost them both.

804
00:58:46,488 --> 00:58:51,916
So, this is what happened with Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(اُمَيَّة بِنْ خَلَف) who is, as Bilal(بلال) said;

805
00:58:52,240 --> 00:58:53,115
إمام في الكفر

806
00:58:53,219 --> 00:58:55,813
He was an Imam(اِمَام) of disbelief.

807
00:58:57,288 --> 00:59:03,861
Anas Ibn Malikرضي الله عنه tells us the story of Al-Qaleeb(ألقليب).

808
00:59:04,320 --> 00:59:10,147
He says; The Messenger of Allah ordered on the day of the battle at Badr(بدر),

809
00:59:10,600 --> 00:59:16,921
that 24 of the chiefs of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) be thrown into a dirty refuse laden old Well.

810
00:59:17,181 --> 00:59:23,310
So, the bodies of the leaders of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), Twenty four of them were dragged into this grave.

811
00:59:23,627 --> 00:59:28,206
It was a dirty, refuse laden old well as Anas Ibn Malik(اَنَس اِبْن مالك) describes it.

812
00:59:29,321 --> 00:59:32,398
When they were pulling the body of Ut'ba Bin Rabiyah(عتبة بن ربيعة).

813
00:59:32,914 --> 00:59:35,477
His son Hudhaifa(حذيفه) was watching on.

814
00:59:36,501 --> 00:59:44,096
So Rasool Allah ﷺ, looks into his face and sees that he was distressed, he was sad.

815
00:59:45,037 --> 00:59:50,309
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Abu Hudhaifah(أبو حذيفه), are you very upset at your father's fate?

816
00:59:51,169 --> 00:59:53,017
So, Abu Hudhaifah(أبو حذيفه) responds back,

817
00:59:53,621 --> 00:59:58,603
I swear, O Messenger of Allah. I have no problems with my father's fate.

818
00:59:59,219 --> 01:00:03,456
But I once knew him as a man of reason, judgment and goodness

819
01:00:04,032 --> 01:00:07,215
and hope those qualities would lead him to Islam.

820
01:00:07,976 --> 01:00:14,070
When I saw, what his fate was and how he had died in disbelief, despite my hopes for him,

821
01:00:14,372 --> 01:00:15,655
I was saddened.

822
01:00:16,377 --> 01:00:19,277
Rasool Allah ﷺ then made Dua(دُعَا) for him.

823
01:00:19,976 --> 01:00:21,485
Dear brothers and sisters,

824
01:00:22,715 --> 01:00:26,691
The issue of guidance is something in the hands of Allah, nobody can control it.

825
01:00:27,656 --> 01:00:32,735
Here Abu Hudhaifah(أبو حذيفه) is saying that my father was wise, he was a man of reason.

826
01:00:33,324 --> 01:00:37,735
He was a man of judgment, he was a man of goodness, and I hope that these qualities would guide him to Islam.

827
01:00:39,122 --> 01:00:42,664
But things didn't turn out, as he expected.

828
01:00:43,876 --> 01:00:47,794
And that is the case with Abu Talib(ابو طالب) also,

829
01:00:48,512 --> 01:00:52,184
Abu Talib(ابو طالب) the uncle of Rasool Allah ﷺ carried these same qualities.

830
01:00:52,548 --> 01:00:59,302
In fact, he protected Rasool Allah ﷺ for the entire period he spent in Makkah, until he passed away,

831
01:01:00,374 --> 01:01:02,556
and Abu Talib(ابو طالب) never became Muslim.

832
01:01:03,254 --> 01:01:06,072
So, when it comes to the issue of guidance, you can't really tell

833
01:01:06,704 --> 01:01:08,393
who will be guided and who won't.

834
01:01:08,944 --> 01:01:12,659
While Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), who is so evil in his torture of Muslims,

835
01:01:13,564 --> 01:01:15,084
he becomes Muslim,

836
01:01:15,664 --> 01:01:17,617
and we talked about the story of Islam that

837
01:01:17,957 --> 01:01:24,963
when one of the Muslims saw that one of the Sahabiaat(صحابيات) was expecting Umar(عُمَر) to become Muslim,

838
01:01:25,003 --> 01:01:27,733
because he spoke to her softly.

839
01:01:27,996 --> 01:01:32,322
He responded back by saying the donkey of his father would become a Muslim before he does.

840
01:01:33,204 --> 01:01:38,183
Meaning take that idea out of your mind such a person can never become Muslim, but he did.

841
01:01:38,585 --> 01:01:40,355
And he became one of the best Muslims.

842
01:01:41,094 --> 01:01:45,210
So the issue of who is guided and who isn't is something that we cannot control.

843
01:01:45,440 --> 01:01:47,173
And we cannot even expect.

844
01:01:47,484 --> 01:01:50,996
Don't make a judgment on a person and say O, he might become Muslim,

845
01:01:51,194 --> 01:01:53,461
and O, he might not become Muslim.

846
01:01:54,310 --> 01:01:59,647
You know, at the end, Abu Talib(ابو طالب) dies as a Kafir(كافر) and Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) dies as a Muslim.

847
01:02:00,724 --> 01:02:05,560
Abu Talib(ابو طالب), who supports Rasool Allahﷺ for all of his life ends up going to Hellfire.

848
01:02:05,897 --> 01:02:10,909
While Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان), who fights Rasool Allah ﷺ for most of his life ends up becoming Muslim.

849
01:02:11,654 --> 01:02:14,848
So, such issues should be left in the hands of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

850
01:02:15,078 --> 01:02:16,710
And that's why, Rasool Allah ﷺ says,

851
01:02:16,734 --> 01:02:19,488
إِنَّكَ لا تَهْدِي مَنْ أَحْبَبْتَ وَلَكِنَّ اللَّهَ يَهْدِي مَنْ يَشَاءُ

852
01:02:19,905 --> 01:02:23,787
You don't guide the ones you want, the ones you love, the ones you like,

853
01:02:24,041 --> 01:02:26,985
but it is Allah who guides, the ones He wants.

854
01:02:27,414 --> 01:02:31,270
This is a matter of Qadar( قدر) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ and we'll leave it in His hands.

855
01:02:31,974 --> 01:02:35,000
So, Abu Hudhaifah(أبو حذيفه) here was kind of upset and sad

856
01:02:35,933 --> 01:02:38,627
because his father didn't become Muslim.

857
01:02:39,174 --> 01:02:43,568
It also shows you, our loyalty should go to Allah entirely.

858
01:02:44,044 --> 01:02:49,679
And even though Abu Hudhaifah(أبوحذيفه) was sad that his father died as a disbeliever

859
01:02:50,622 --> 01:02:57,581
But that didn't make him forsake his religion, or blame someone or blame something

860
01:02:57,899 --> 01:02:59,438
that my father didn't become Muslim.

861
01:02:59,478 --> 01:03:05,345
He accepted it and he said, O Messenger of Allah, I have no problems with my father's fate, I accept it.

862
01:03:05,715 --> 01:03:08,234
I accept that this is from Allahعَزّوجَلّ, I accept it.

863
01:03:08,392 --> 01:03:09,028
And this is called;

864
01:03:09,077 --> 01:03:10,377
رِضَى بِقَدَرِ الله عَزُّواَجَلْ

865
01:03:10,463 --> 01:03:14,427
You're content with what Allahعَزّوجَلّ gives you and what happens to you.

866
01:03:15,215 --> 01:03:22,107
And I'm saying this because we've known brothers and sisters in the West, who have embraced Islam

867
01:03:22,287 --> 01:03:23,975
but their parents didn't.

868
01:03:24,247 --> 01:03:29,247
And they are very eager to have their parents become Muslim, and they are giving them Da'wah(دعوة).

869
01:03:29,554 --> 01:03:32,575
I just want to say that you do your best in Da'wah(دعوة)

870
01:03:32,757 --> 01:03:35,295
but then leave the issue of Hidayah(هدايه), in the hands of Allah

871
01:03:35,517 --> 01:03:42,333
and don't become overwhelmed or upset, if they don't die as Muslim

872
01:03:42,586 --> 01:03:44,698
and accepted as the Qadar(قدر) of Allahعَزّوجَل.

873
01:03:44,928 --> 01:03:48,573
And if they do become Muslim, then give credit to Allahعَزّوجَلّ

874
01:03:48,885 --> 01:03:54,087
and leave it in his hands and say, Al-Hamdolillah(إلحمدلله) that Allahعَزّوجَلّ has guided them to His religion.

875
01:03:54,417 --> 01:03:57,314
Rasool Allah ﷺ tried very hard with his uncle, but it didn't work.

876
01:03:58,327 --> 01:04:02,809
While people from distant lands would come to him like Salman  Farsi(سلمان فارسي), and Abu Dhar(أبو زر).

877
01:04:02,965 --> 01:04:05,491
We asked Allahعَزّوجَلّ to guide us to the truth.

878
01:04:06,447 --> 01:04:13,242
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ ordered that the bodies of 24 of the chiefs of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) be thrown into this well.

879
01:04:13,919 --> 01:04:23,306
Rasool Allah ﷺ, it was his habit that he would stay at the site of the battle for three days, before he would leave.

880
01:04:24,522 --> 01:04:28,200
When he was about to leave from the site of the Battle of Badr(بدر).

881
01:04:28,486 --> 01:04:36,746
He visited the Qulaib(قليب), this Well in which the 24 leaders of Kuffr(كفر) were buried.

882
01:04:37,738 --> 01:04:39,241
And he was speaking to them, He said;

883
01:04:39,733 --> 01:04:44,892
Would you now, be pleased to have obeyed Allah and His messenger?

884
01:04:45,655 --> 01:04:49,461
We have found that what our Lord promised us was true.

885
01:04:49,882 --> 01:04:53,461
Have you found what your Lord promised you to be true?

886
01:04:55,398 --> 01:04:57,320
Umar Ibn Al-Khattabرضي الله عنه said;

887
01:04:57,439 --> 01:05:02,312
 O, Messenger of Allah, why do you speak to bodies that have no spirits in them?

888
01:05:02,757 --> 01:05:08,017
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: by Him, Who holds the soul of Muhammad(محمد) in His hand,

889
01:05:08,380 --> 01:05:12,178
You do not hear, what I say any better than they do.

890
01:05:12,384 --> 01:05:13,527
And this is in Bukhari(بخاريْ),

891
01:05:14,080 --> 01:05:19,654
so Allahعَزّوجَلّ made them hear, what Rasool Allah ﷺ was telling them.

892
01:05:20,618 --> 01:05:23,118
And this is to add to their punishment.

893
01:05:23,991 --> 01:05:27,862
رَبَّنَا آتِنَا فِي الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً وَفِي الْآخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً وَقِنَا عَذَابَ النَّارِ۝

894
01:05:28,149 --> 01:05:32,550
وَصَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

895
01:05:32,851 --> 01:05:35,462
وَالسلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

